## Data Flow: Expense Split & Settlement

```
Trip has 3 members: A, B, C

Expenses added:
  Expense 1: ₹3,000 paid by A, EQUAL split (A, B, C) → each owes ₹1,000
  Expense 2: ₹6,000 paid by B, EQUAL split (A, B, C) → each owes ₹2,000
  Expense 3: ₹1,500 paid by C, EQUAL split (A, B)    → each owes ₹750

Calculate net balances:
  A: paid ₹3,000  owes ₹1,000+₹2,000+₹750 = ₹3,750   net = -₹750
  B: paid ₹6,000  owes ₹1,000+₹2,000       = ₹3,000   net = +₹3,000
  C: paid ₹1,500  owes ₹1,000+₹2,000       = ₹3,000   net = -₹1,500

Settle Up (simplified):
  C owes most (-₹1,500) → pays B ₹1,500   → B = +₹1,500, C = 0
  A owes (-₹750)        → pays B ₹750     → B = +₹750,   A = 0
  B gets ₹0 remaining   → done ✓

Result: 2 transactions, all settled
```
